1}=-3$ and $det(A)=8$\n\nII. $A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite\n\nIII. $a$ is a local maximum of $f$" :question/worked-solution "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nIn this case, we have $A={f}^{″}(a).$ Now, before we examine the statements, let's recall how to categorize quadratic forms.\n\nLet ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-3$ and\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}|=8.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-3<0, \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}|=8>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the matrix $A$ is negative-definite.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the matrix $A$ is negative-definite, the critical point $a$ is a local maximum of $f.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-aabf5329-c030-5348-b4b6-66587320416f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-aabf5329-c030-5348-b4b6-66587320416f" :answer-field/id #uuid "aabf5329-c030-5348-b4b6-66587320416f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1344f994-c7f3-5ec5-8bc3-dd5fb9f3b026" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1344f994-c7f3-5ec5-8bc3-dd5fb9f3b026" "answer-9be9a2ae-0d17-5397-99d7-af0f171bb5f2" "answer-f49e2cba-f810-5365-a372-e6f45bdb78dc" "answer-a028efe8-76c4-5c04-82bd-e900a7c72295" "answer-9bd164ff-c783-54c1-a435-26f55abca16c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1344f994-c7f3-5ec5-8bc3-dd5fb9f3b026" :answer/id #uuid "1344f994-c7f3-5ec5-8bc3-dd5fb9f3b026" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9be9a2ae-0d17-5397-99d7-af0f171bb5f2" :answer/id #uuid "9be9a2ae-0d17-5397-99d7-af0f171bb5f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f49e2cba-f810-5365-a372-e6f45bdb78dc" :answer/id #uuid "f49e2cba-f810-5365-a372-e6f45bdb78dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a028efe8-76c4-5c04-82bd-e900a7c72295" :answer/id #uuid "a028efe8-76c4-5c04-82bd-e900a7c72295" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bd164ff-c783-54c1-a435-26f55abca16c" :answer/id #uuid "9bd164ff-c783-54c1-a435-26f55abca16c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e5518b1c-8ee2-55b4-900e-3e5d5d3b8c0e" :question/id #uuid "e5518b1c-8ee2-55b4-900e-3e5d5d3b8c0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-163788" :question/problem "The quadratic Taylor approximation of the function $f(x)$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{3}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈1+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}A(x-a),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${a}_{11}=-1$ and $det(A)=-15$\n\nII. $A$ is negative-definite\n\nIII. $a$ is a local minimum of $f$" :question/worked-solution "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nIn this case, we have $A={f}^{″}(a).$ Now, before we examine the statements, we recall how to categorize quadratic forms.\n\nLet ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-1,$ but\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1(3)-4(4)+2(-6) \\\\  & =-31.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-1<0 \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|=-19<0 \\\\ {Δ}_{3} & =|A|=-31<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the matrix $A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the matrix $A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, the critical point $a$ is a saddle point of $f.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-87f2c732-43a9-5f28-96fb-2493dab452dc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-87f2c732-43a9-5f28-96fb-2493dab452dc" :answer-field/id #uuid "87f2c732-43a9-5f28-96fb-2493dab452dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f3ed4b64-e1dd-5cfc-b0b1-4c2ef452329a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1b15bd6b-53d9-5f2c-a622-474fbfa83e12" "answer-a7339b2b-0cd2-58b2-bb3e-d169ebbe1f97" "answer-c1745eb2-62cc-52f0-8eb2-e37d4282fc2d" "answer-b6d79cac-7978-5207-995a-d295dee5e728" "answer-f3ed4b64-e1dd-5cfc-b0b1-4c2ef452329a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b15bd6b-53d9-5f2c-a622-474fbfa83e12" :answer/id #uuid "1b15bd6b-53d9-5f2c-a622-474fbfa83e12" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7339b2b-0cd2-58b2-bb3e-d169ebbe1f97" :answer/id #uuid "a7339b2b-0cd2-58b2-bb3e-d169ebbe1f97" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c1745eb2-62cc-52f0-8eb2-e37d4282fc2d" :answer/id #uuid "c1745eb2-62cc-52f0-8eb2-e37d4282fc2d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6d79cac-7978-5207-995a-d295dee5e728" :answer/id #uuid "b6d79cac-7978-5207-995a-d295dee5e728" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3ed4b64-e1dd-5cfc-b0b1-4c2ef452329a" :answer/id #uuid "f3ed4b64-e1dd-5cfc-b0b1-4c2ef452329a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}]
